// The node settings of both stack sweep nodes (P7-8), merged over the corpus defaults.json. The run
// sets local_address, prng_seed, drc.default_speed and drc.table; everything else is here, and the
// whole merged record goes into each run's result. Changing a value here changes every result, so a
// sweep records this file in its plan.json and a resumed run refuses a different one.
//
// Choices (ours, for P7-9 to revisit with the measured turnaround and EOT overshoot):
// - CSMA (coordinator ruling 2026-11-08, from the P7-9b contention measurements in
//   docs/stack-sweep.md): 8 contention slots of 3 s, 2 s after DCD, 3 s after VDCD. Two nodes on one
//   channel never need the standard's 16 slots and 30 s listen-before-talk [Ed4 K Table 7, p.K-12];
//   with those, turnaround and not the rung would set the throughput. With 1 s slots and a 0.5 s VDCD
//   wait equal or adjacent draws collided on slow rungs; 8 slots of 3 s with VDCD 3 s gave 2 to 3
//   overlaps per 1800 s run. (P7-8 to P7-9b used the bench's 4 slots of 1 s and VDCD 0.5 s.)
// - Transmissions of at most 30 s. The standard's 127.5 s (K-0094) would let a single slow
//   transmission run for minutes; the bench's 6 s is shorter than one Long block on WN 1 and 2.
//   The answer wait is left derived: 30 s + 3 s + 8 x 3 s = 57 s.
// - Links: as the bench (4 links, 5 link request retries, 3 break retries).
{
  "csma": { "mode": "jitter", "num_cont_slots": 8, "cont_slot_width_ms": 3000, "lbt_wait_dcd_ms": 2000, "lbt_wait_vdcd_ms": 3000 },
  "dts": { "max_transmission_ms": 30000 },
  "cas": { "max_links": 4, "link_request_retries": 5, "break_retries": 3 }
}
